request: Make the output easier to read. --behaviour

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different output changes, and I can't write a test for it without knowing which one you want. Right now `todo list` prints only "[ ] buy milk" / "[x] walk dog". It doesn't show ids or due dates, even though they're stored and you need the id for `todo complete`.)
governor asks: Which of these should "easier to read" mean? Pick any that apply, or describe the layout you want:
(a) Show each todo's id in `todo list`, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk".
(b) Show due dates, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)".
(c) Line the columns up so ids, titles and due dates sit under each other.
(d) Put open todos first and done ones last, or sort by due date.
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. "2 open, 1 done".
(f) Change other messages too, like "Added #1" or the error text.
If you'd like a sensible default, I'd do (a), (b) and (c) only.

